claim_iheap_compat	Since undo is kept in extents of the table's own main fork, WAL, crash recovery, replicas, backups and logical replication work for iheap as for any table	thesis	result	{iheap,undo_log}
claim_iheap_no_bloat	A long-running transaction with frequent updates stops being a big problem: iheap tables do not bloat the way heap does	argument	conclusion	{bloat,heap,iheap}
claim_iheap_no_core_patch	In-place update, similar in idea to zheap, was done without a core patch: in PostgreSQL 19 the standard mechanisms are enough for it, from a resource manager of its own to visibility horizons	thesis	result	{iheap,inplace_update,zheap}
