id	text	role	about
claim_citus_hydra_rows	Citus columnar and Hydra are columnar inside, but through the tableAM API they hand out slots one row at a time	example	{citus_columnar,hydra_columnar,table_access_method}
claim_custom_glue	MergeTree cannot be built into PostgreSQL by simple linking: a glue layer of its own was needed	thesis	{ch_table_engines,libchte_engine,mergetree}
claim_final_result	PostgreSQL 19 with the author's extensions runs ClickBench only a few times slower than ClickHouse on the same machine while keeping PostgreSQL's replicas, pg_dump and MVCC	counterexample	{ch_table_engines,obs_final_ch,obs_final_pg,pg_vexec,postgresql}
claim_iheap_compat	Since undo is kept in extents of the table's own main fork, WAL, crash recovery, replicas, backups and logical replication work for iheap as for any table	thesis	{iheap,undo_log}
claim_iheap_no_bloat	A long-running transaction with frequent updates stops being a big problem: iheap tables do not bloat the way heap does	argument	{bloat,heap,iheap}
claim_iheap_no_core_patch	In-place update, similar in idea to zheap, was done without a core patch: in PostgreSQL 19 the standard mechanisms are enough for it, from a resource manager of its own to visibility horizons	thesis	{iheap,inplace_update,zheap}
claim_no_columnar_source	On unmodified PostgreSQL 19 there is not a single storage that would hand the vectorized executor data column by column	argument	{columnar_storage,pg_vexec,table_access_method}
claim_row_locks_undo	Row locks in iheap are also kept as undo records, so neither MultiXact nor freezing is needed	thesis	{freezing,iheap,multixact,undo_log}
claim_tableam_row_api	PostgreSQL's table API hands out rows one at a time through a slot and does not accept a list of the needed columns, and heap offers no extension point to skip unneeded pages	argument	{heap,table_access_method}
claim_use_case	PostgreSQL with extensions suits a huge metrics table with hundreds of columns next to transactional data from different systems and joins between tables, all in one transaction	argument	{ch_table_engines,mergetree,postgresql}
